---
description: |
  Summarizes HarfangLab Network Activity (`class_uid` 4001) into one event per
  window, host, local and remote IP address, service port, protocol, and
  direction. Listen events (`activity_id` 7) get summaries per bind address
  and port. Events of other classes pass through unchanged.

  Each summary is a Network Activity event with the OCSF aggregation
  attributes: `count` holds the number of connections, `start_time` and
  `end_time` the times of the first and last one, `duration` the time between
  them, and `time` equals `start_time`. All times are epoch milliseconds, like
  HarfangLab's.

  HarfangLab describes every connection from the endpoint's point of view:
  `src_endpoint` is the local end and `dst_endpoint` the remote end. The
  service port is therefore `src_endpoint.port` for inbound connections and
  `dst_endpoint.port` otherwise, and the summary keeps it there. The client
  port appears only if all connections of the summary had the same one, so
  the summary of a single connection keeps it.

  The key also covers the activity, severity, status, and the agent
  identity of the endpoints. The summary takes the device, the metadata, and
  the agent lists from the first event of the host with the same key values
  in the window.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing, the memory it needs, and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: Width of the summary windows, in processing and event time.
---

// `$window` names the argument only outside the `window` block.
if class_uid == 4001 {
  _host = device?.agent_list?[0]?.uid? else device?.hostname?
  _bucket = from_epoch(time? * 1ms).floor($window)
  _inbound = connection_info?.direction_id? == 1
  _service_port = src_endpoint?.port? if _inbound else dst_endpoint?.port?
  _client_port = dst_endpoint?.port? if _inbound else src_endpoint?.port?
  // Every group key and aggregate costs memory per summary. The values in
  // `_ids` are few per host, so the summaries group by their digest and take
  // them from one context record per host and digest. The device, metadata,
  // and agent lists belong to the host and come from the first event of the
  // context.
  _ids = hash_xxh3([device?.hostname?, activity_id?, activity_name?,
    severity_id?, severity?, status_id?, status?, type_uid?,
    connection_info?.direction_id?, connection_info?.direction?,
    connection_info?.protocol_name?, connection_info?.protocol_num?,
    connection_info?.protocol_ver_id?, src_endpoint?.name?,
    src_endpoint?.uid?, src_endpoint?.hostname?, dst_endpoint?.name?,
    dst_endpoint?.uid?, dst_endpoint?.hostname?])
  window size=$window {
    fork_merge {
      summarize _host, _bucket, _ids, src_endpoint?.ip?, dst_endpoint?.ip?,
        _service_port,
        count=count(), start_time=min(time?), end_time=max(time?),
        _client_port_min=min(_client_port), _client_port_max=max(_client_port),
        _client_port_count=count(_client_port)
    }, {
      summarize _host, _ids, _context=first({
        activity_id: activity_id?,
        activity_name: activity_name?,
        severity: severity?,
        severity_id: severity_id?,
        status: status?,
        status_id: status_id?,
        type_uid: type_uid?,
        metadata: metadata?,
        device: device?,
        connection_info: {
          direction_id: connection_info?.direction_id?,
          direction: connection_info?.direction?,
          protocol_name: connection_info?.protocol_name?,
          protocol_num: connection_info?.protocol_num?,
          protocol_ver_id: connection_info?.protocol_ver_id?,
        },
        src_endpoint: {
          name: src_endpoint?.name?,
          uid: src_endpoint?.uid?,
          hostname: src_endpoint?.hostname?,
          agent_list: src_endpoint?.agent_list?,
        },
        dst_endpoint: {
          name: dst_endpoint?.name?,
          uid: dst_endpoint?.uid?,
          hostname: dst_endpoint?.hostname?,
          agent_list: dst_endpoint?.agent_list?,
        },
      })
    }
    // The context of a host and digest sorts before its summaries, so a
    // running `first` hands it to each of them.
    sort _host, _ids, _context? == null
    summarize _host, _ids, _ctx=first(_context?),
      options={mode: "cumulative"}
    where _context? == null
    _inbound = _ctx.connection_info.direction_id == 1
    _client_port = (_client_port_min
      if _client_port_min == _client_port_max
        and _client_port_count == count else null)
    this = {
      activity_id: _ctx.activity_id,
      activity_name: _ctx.activity_name,
      category_uid: 4,
      class_uid: 4001,
      metadata: _ctx.metadata,
      severity: _ctx.severity,
      severity_id: _ctx.severity_id,
      status: _ctx.status,
      status_id: _ctx.status_id,
      time: start_time,
      start_time: start_time,
      end_time: end_time,
      duration: end_time - start_time,
      count: count,
      type_uid: _ctx.type_uid,
      device: _ctx.device,
      connection_info: _ctx.connection_info,
      src_endpoint: {
        ..._ctx.src_endpoint,
        ip: src_endpoint.ip,
        port: _service_port if _inbound else _client_port,
      },
      dst_endpoint: {
        ..._ctx.dst_endpoint,
        ip: dst_endpoint.ip,
        port: _client_port if _inbound else _service_port,
      },
    }
    drop_null_fields
  }
}
